  "generated": "2026-09-27T03:21:11",
  "dataset": {
    "name": "google/fleurs test split (local pinned copy)",
    "path": "evaluation\\fleurs_test_100",
    "revision": "70bb2e84b976b7e960aa89f1c648e09c59f894dd",
    "samples_per_language": 30,
    "selection": "manifest.csv rows for the language, sorted by audio_path, first N (deterministic)",
    "note": "Read speech. Kathbath/IndicVoices audio is not present in this project, so FLEURS was used."
  },
  "normalization": "Unicode NFC, casefold (lowercase), every Unicode punctuation (P*) and symbol (S*) character replaced with a space, then whitespace collapsed and stripped. Indic combining marks are preserved. WER computed with jiwer.wer() on whitespace-separated tokens of the normalized strings.",
  "metrics": {
    "WER": "percent, jiwer.wer() over normalized whitespace tokens, corpus-level",
    "RTF": "sum(per-sample inference seconds) / sum(audio seconds); excludes model load and audio decode",
    "peak_RAM_MB": "peak process RSS sampled at 50 ms across model load + inference, one model per process",
    "disk_MB": "on-disk size of the weights actually loaded"
  },
  "caveats": [
    "RTF is not a pure architecture comparison: the multilingual model runs as ONNX Runtime graphs (operator-fused, release-optimized) while the monolingual model runs as eager PyTorch/NeMo. WER is unaffected by this; RTF favours the multilingual runtime.",
    "Decoders differ: multilingual is CTC with a per-language vocabulary mask (the only path this project ships); the monolingual hybrid is decoded with its own head.",
    "CPU-only, 4 threads, to approximate phone-class compute rather than the dev GPU.",
    "INT8 (131 MB) variants were NOT benchmarked: onnxruntime 1.23.2 CPU has no ConvInteger kernel for the int8 weights this export uses (MatMulInteger u8s8 is fine, ConvInteger is not), so the session fails to initialize. All monolingual numbers here are FP32 (459.7 MB).",
    "Monolingual is decoded with the CTC head only (the ONNX export is nemo-conformer-ctc). The hybrid checkpoint RNNT head is unmeasured, so monolingual WER here is a conservative floor.",
    "MatMul-only INT8 is FASTER than FP32 here (RTF ~0.020 vs ~0.050), not slower. Reports of dynamic INT8 being ~3x slower come from Conv/ConvTranspose-heavy graphs such as VITS vocoders; a Conformer encoder is MatMul-dominated, so quantising MatMul moves the bulk of the compute onto integer kernels.",
    "Peak RAM figures include ~500 MB of desktop PyTorch that an Android build does not load (measured separately: `import torch` alone is +498 MB). On-device footprint will be lower; these are upper bounds, and no on-device measurement has been taken yet."
  ],
